From 60e36ded853dd4afed99cb78c5a8d7d71be162e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: boromyr <52782032+boromyr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:12:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add dark theme

Add war/dark-theme.css, loaded by circuitjs.html, which restyles the
GWT widgets, menus, dialogs and side panel in dark colors.

To make the theme possible without matching inline styles, move the
hardcoded UI colors out of the Java code:
- Toolbar and SubcircuitBar use CSS classes (cirjs-toolbar*, palette-container)
  instead of inline colors and JS hover handlers; the light defaults
  live in style.css and match the previous look.
- Scrollbar reads its drawing colors from --cirjs-scrollbar-* CSS
  variables, falling back to the previous colors.
- ShortcutsDialog clears the text color instead of forcing black.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

