From 2648551d98811ba489e410b1c416e0a1ab022265 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: boromyr <52782032+boromyr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:41:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix singular matrix in PeltierElm on master's split-matrix
 solver

master partitions the circuit into independent matrices using
getMatrixConnection(), which defaults to getConnection(). PeltierElm
(from pfalstad/circuitjs1#385, written against v3-dev) only connects
posts 0-1 and 2-3, so its internal node ended up in a different matrix
than the Seebeck voltage source's other node, and the thermoelectric
examples stopped with "Singular matrix!".

Keep all its nodes in one matrix, as TransformerElm and VCCSElm do,
since the Seebeck/Peltier terms couple the electrical and thermal sides.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/com/lushprojects/circuitjs1/client/PeltierElm.java b/src/com/lushprojects/circuitjs1/client/PeltierElm.java
index 03cf1356..666cfb9a 100644
--- a/src/com/lushprojects/circuitjs1/client/PeltierElm.java
+++ b/src/com/lushprojects/circuitjs1/client/PeltierElm.java
@@ -161,6 +161,9 @@ class PeltierElm extends CircuitElm {
 	if ((n1 == 2 && n2 == 3) || (n1 == 3 && n2 == 2)) return true;
 	return false;
     }
+    // the Seebeck/Peltier terms couple the electrical, thermal and internal nodes,
+    // so they must all be in the same matrix
+    boolean getMatrixConnection(int n1, int n2) { return true; }
 
     void stamp() {
 	// electrical: Seebeck source (nodes 0 -> internal 4) in series with R (4 -> 1)

From 7466b16dfebb28a78c97ccd44b06c62f161dee0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: boromyr <52782032+boromyr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:45:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add J201 JFET model, fix BETA conversion in SPICE import

Add a built-in "J201" N-channel JFET model from the Fairchild SPICE
model (Vto=-0.5961, Beta=1.304m, Lambda=2.4m, Cgs=4.442p, Cgd=4.48p).

SPICE uses Ids = BETA*(Vgs-VTO)^2 while this simulator uses
Ids = beta/2*(Vgs-Vt)^2, so beta = 2*BETA. The SPICE subcircuit import
passed BETA through unchanged, giving JFETs half the drain current;
convert it there too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/com/lushprojects/circuitjs1/client/ImportFromSpiceDialog.java b/src/com/lushprojects/circuitjs1/client/ImportFromSpiceDialog.java
index a9872024..8a3e785b 100644
--- a/src/com/lushprojects/circuitjs1/client/ImportFromSpiceDialog.java
+++ b/src/com/lushprojects/circuitjs1/client/ImportFromSpiceDialog.java
@@ -232,7 +232,8 @@ TextArea outputArea;
 				if (s.startsWith("vto="))
 				    fm.vto = parseNumber(s.substring(4));
 				else if (s.startsWith("beta="))
-				    fm.beta = parseNumber(s.substring(5));
+				    // SPICE: Ids = BETA*(Vgs-VTO)^2; JfetElm: Ids = beta/2*(Vgs-Vt)^2
+				    fm.beta = 2*parseNumber(s.substring(5));
 			    }
 			    fetModels.put(name, fm);
 			}
diff --git a/src/com/lushprojects/circuitjs1/client/MosfetModel.java b/src/com/lushprojects/circuitjs1/client/MosfetModel.java
index 899cecd7..06617271 100644
--- a/src/com/lushprojects/circuitjs1/client/MosfetModel.java
+++ b/src/com/lushprojects/circuitjs1/client/MosfetModel.java
@@ -132,6 +132,17 @@ public class MosfetModel implements Editable, Comparable<MosfetModel> {
 	MosfetModel jfetDefault = new MosfetModel("default-jfet", -4, .00125).setJfet();
 	jfetDefault.showBulk = jfetDefault.bodyDiode = false;
 	addDefaultModel("default-jfet", jfetDefault);
+
+	// J201 N-channel JFET, from the Fairchild SPICE model:
+	// .model J201 NJF(Beta=1.304m Lambda=2.4m Vto=-.5961 Cgd=4.48p Cgs=4.442p ...)
+	// SPICE uses Ids = BETA*(Vgs-VTO)^2, this simulator Ids = beta/2*(Vgs-Vt)^2, so beta = 2*BETA.
+	// (junction caps are constant here, SPICE's voltage dependence M/PB is not modeled)
+	MosfetModel j201 = new MosfetModel("J201", -.5961, 2*1.304e-3).setJfet();
+	j201.lambda = 2.4e-3;
+	j201.capGS = 4.442e-12;
+	j201.capGD = 4.48e-12;
+	j201.showBulk = j201.bodyDiode = false;
+	addDefaultModel("J201", j201);
     }
 
     static void addDefaultModel(String name, MosfetModel dm) {

From 32f485ceb865ba53a080385601f749f43f02fa5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: boromyr <52782032+boromyr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:45:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add Bode plot with small-signal AC analysis

New ACAnalysis computes the frequency response of the running circuit,
linearized at its operating point: after a converged timestep the matrix
of a nonlinear circuit is the Newton Jacobian, so transistors, JFETs,
op-amps and any stage after a tone stack are included. Elements with
timestep-dependent companion models replace them with their admittance
in the new CircuitElm.stampAC(): capacitors, inductors, transformers,
diode/BJT junction caps and MOSFET/JFET gate caps (composites forward
to their children).

With a large input the operating point moves during the signal period,
so while the plot is open the Jacobian of a nonlinear circuit is
averaged over one period of the input, after removing the companion
conductances so the average does not depend on the timestep.

The Bode window (war/bodeplot.js, ported from the local Electron build)
gets its data through CircuitJS1.getACTargets()/acSweep() and is opened
from Scopes > Bode Plot... or Bode in the menu bar. It shows magnitude
and unwrapped phase, held traces, offset and CSV export, in English or
Italian. app/main.js allows its child window in Electron, and makeSite
copies bodeplot.js.

Checked against an RC low-pass (-3.01 dB/-45 deg at fc) and against
transient measurements of a tone stack + JFET stage (within 0.01 dB).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/app/main.js b/app/main.js
